# Product-harness README

This repo targets a **product-level local harness** on pydantic-ai. When editing
`README.md` / `README_CN.md`, match peer harness READMEs (DeepSeek Harness,
OpenHands, Goose, Omnigent) — not a library design doc.

## Page order (do not reorder)

1. **Hero** — name, EN/CN switch, one-sentence product claim (who + outcome),
   optional status line; link strip only for files that exist
   (`Docs` / `Safety` / `Contributing` — do not invent broken links)
2. **Run** — shortest path to a running UI (`uv sync …` → `agent`)
3. **Launch paths** — from source now; add uv-tool / Docker only when shipped;
   each path states prerequisites in one line
4. **What you get** — 4–6 user outcomes (not module names)
5. **Boundaries** — short architecture/ownership table; explicit non-goals
6. **Configure** — `.env` / MCP / models *after* first run (optional, collapsible
   tone); never block the Run section
7. **Programmatic / deep docs** — pointer + tiny snippet; detail in
   `src/*/README.md` or `docs/` when present
8. **License / community**

## Voice

- Lead with **outcome** (“local general agent harness…”), not the type name.
- Prefer **commands the reader can paste** over prose about internals.
- Keep EN and CN **section-parallel**; do not let one language grow a private
  architecture essay.
- Put long “how Supervisor works” narrative in docs; README keeps ≤1 short
  paragraph + link.
- Screenshots prove the Run path; they do not replace it.

## Borrow / skip (from peers)

```text
✅ Goose/DeepSeek: hero + one-command run; architecture in docs/
✅ OpenHands: multi-path quickstart + filesystem/safety warnings + repo-boundary table
✅ Omnigent: “Why” as user outcomes; YAML example after you can start
✅ DeepSeek: preview/breaking-change + SAFETY.md before Run
❌ Architecture / Features / env wall before any Run command
❌ Feature bullets that only name modules (`harness.mcp`, `PlaybookSpec`)
❌ Mid-page essays that belong in AGENTS.md or architecture.md
```

## Shape checklist

| Section | Passes when |
| --- | --- |
| Hero | A stranger knows the product in one sentence without reading Architecture |
| Run | ≤3 commands from clone/install to `http://127.0.0.1:8000` |
| Outcomes | Bullets a non-contributor would care about |
| Boundaries | Table of layers + “deliberately not …” non-goals |
| Configure | Credentials optional or clearly “for X specialist” |

## Exemplar hero (tone)

```markdown
# agent-playbook

Local general-purpose agent harness on [pydantic-ai](https://ai.pydantic.dev/):
YAML specialists (MCP + skills), one web entry via Supervisor.
```

Then **Run**, not Architecture. Add Safety/Docs badges only after those files exist.
